  "generated_text": "1. The volume \\( V \\) of a cylinder is given by:\n   \\[\n   V = \\pi R^2 H\n   \\]\n\n2. The total surface area \\( A \\) of a cylinder is given by:\n   \\[\n   A = 2\\pi R (R + H)\n   \\]\n\n3. To minimize the surface area, we need to find the ratio \\( \\frac{H}{R} \\).\n\n4. From the volume equation, we can express \\( H \\) in terms of \\( R \\):\n   \\[\n   H = \\frac{V}{\\pi R^2}\n   \\]\n\n5. Substitute \\( H \\) into the surface area equation:\n   \\[\n   A = 2\\pi R \\left( R + \\frac{V}{\\pi R^2} \\right)\n   \\]\n\n6. To minimize the surface area, we need to find the ratio \\( \\frac{H}{R} \\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{H}{R} = \\frac{\\frac{V}{\\pi R^2}}{R} = \\frac{V}{\\pi R^3}\n   \\]\n\n\\boxed{2}",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[2, '2']",
    "gold_answer": "For radius $r$ and height $h,$ the volume is given by $\\pi r^2 h = V,$ and the total surface area is given by\n\\[A = 2 \\pi r^2 + 2 \\pi rh.\\]By AM-GM,\n\\begin{align*}\nA &= 2 \\pi r^2 + 2 \\pi rh \\\\\n&= 2 \\pi r^2 + \\pi rh + \\pi rh \\\\\n&\\ge 3 \\sqrt[3]{(2 \\pi r^2)(\\pi rh)(\\pi rh)} \\\\\n&= 3 \\sqrt[3]{2 \\pi^3 r^4 h^2}.\n\\end{align*}Since $\\pi r^2 h = V,$ $r^2 h = \\frac{V}{\\pi}.$  Then\n\\[3 \\sqrt[3]{2 \\pi^3 r^4 h^2} = 3 \\sqrt[3]{2 \\pi^3 \\cdot \\frac{V^2}{\\pi^2}} = 3 \\sqrt[3]{2 \\pi V^2}.\\]Equality occurs when $2 \\pi r^2 = \\pi rh,$ so $\\frac{h}{r} = \\boxed{2}.$",
    "is_correct": true
  },
